# EXPECT: nested inside a module-scope block
# ouroboros#199: a define inside a module-scope loop body is not lifted (the
# lift runs over function bodies), so it reached the statement emitter raw
# and the refusal named the AST node ("cannot emit statement node 'func'").
# Now named. The VM runs it (36) -- and would die on a post-loop call of
# `inner`, which is loop-scoped there.
acc is 0
for x in [1, 2, 3]:
    define inner(d) as:
        return x + d
    acc is acc + (inner of 10)
print of acc
